      <description>&lt;h1 id=&#34;no-mind-nathan-gill&#34;&gt;No Mind Nathan Gill&lt;/h1&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Source: &lt;a href=&#34;https://www.advaita.org.uk/discourses/teachers/nomind_gill.htm&#34;&gt;TW&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Author: Nathan Gill&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;http://www.amazon.co.uk/exec/obidos/ASIN/0954779223/thespiritupat-21&#34;&gt;&lt;figure class=&#34;&#34;&gt;&#xA;&#xA;    &lt;a href=&#34;https://www.advaita.org.uk/images/awake_gill.jpg&#34; target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;&gt;&#xA;        &lt;img src=&#34;https://www.advaita.org.uk/images/awake_gill.jpg&#34; alt=&#34;&#34; title=&#34;&#34;&gt;&#xA;    &lt;/a&gt;&#xA;&#xA;    &#xA;&#xA;&lt;/figure&gt;&#xA;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Visit &lt;a href=&#34;http://www.nathangill.com&#34;&gt;Nathan Gill &amp;rsquo;s website.&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Link to entry on &lt;a href=&#34;https://www.advaita.org.uk/teachers/neo_teachers1.htm#nathan&#34;&gt;Current Teacher&amp;rsquo;s page&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;See &lt;a href=&#34;https://www.advaita.org.uk/reading/read_neo.htm#gill&#34;&gt;Book Recommendation&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;The following is an Extract from ‘Afternoon Talk, Kensington, London. June 2004’ from the above book ‘Already Awake: Dialogues with Nathan Gill’, Non-Duality Press, Sept. 2004, ISBN 0-9547792-2-3.) It can be purchased from &lt;a href=&#34;http://www.non-dualitybooks.com&#34;&gt;Non-Duality Books&lt;/a&gt; in the UK. Also available from &lt;a href=&#34;http://www.amazon.co.uk/exec/obidos/ASIN/0954779223/thespiritupat-21&#34;&gt;Amazon.uk&lt;/a&gt; and &lt;a href=&#34;http://www.amazon.com/exec/obidos/ASIN/0954779223/fromtheunreat-20&#34;&gt;Amazon.com&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Q: So there is this body-mind and a thought arises - for instance, ‘I am hungry’ - and the brain reacts to that thought.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
